  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nWednesday night we continue our warm and dry pattern as broad \nridging remains over South Central Texas and eventually becomes more \namplified heading into the late week period. Each day will remain \nwarm and above average for highs starting Thursday and continuing \ninto the weekend with mid 80s through Friday. With mid to upper 80s \nover the first half of the weekend before leveling off into the low \n80s for Sunday and through the rest of the extended period. Lows \nwill also remain mild, in the mid to upper 50s through the entire \nforecast period. Additionally, we will see the return of more humid \nconditions then what we currently have with dewpoints back into the \n50s and 60s. \n\nEventually, a trough is expected to move over the western U.S late \nin the period but the elongated upper ridge should limit impacts for \nmost of our area associated with this feature as most long range \nmodels suggest the trough pushing north of our area. The exception \nbeing the Rio Grande and Southern Edwards Plateau regions where just \nenough of a disturbance could clip these areas late in the weekend. \nHowever, confidence continues to remain fairly low as pops are only \nin the 20% to 30% range for now. Stay tuned.",
